#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9734fc0-9789-5a9c-8ae0-806f87052875" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db7f23fb-a46d-509e-a8c6-6e56209583c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = i - 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168458} {:answer/id #uuid "fa51b6ef-1535-5853-bd6e-e98cb26fb3c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x, y) =-i + j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168459} {:answer/id #uuid "fca0757b-b187-5d2f-be6d-e22b5c949774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x, y) =-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168460} {:answer/id #uuid "71c400f3-5dba-507b-9730-2e4291e3db20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x, y) = i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168461} {:answer/id #uuid "7c730434-72fd-520a-833a-0af4a368c78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa51b6ef-1535-5853-bd6e-e98cb26fb3c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x, y) =-i + j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168459} :answer-field/id #uuid "5616e32c-fc32-5cfd-a967-845ac13a47d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b0d06ed-9894-556b-a427-a46e4623bd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-122463" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/e3614ea1954f36435eb1ab5f52c04d4fa3062ac337eccf76a5b47e4a03a64a1b.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i-2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=-i+j.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9734fc0-9789-5a9c-8ae0-806f87052875" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9fb5b94-5e4d-5e8d-badc-f06e1748045e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355256} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb9413f-2322-5c1a-b080-8bbee476c873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=y\\,i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355257} {:answer/id #uuid "4a704b3c-ce02-53aa-9160-1f264dbf6080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=x\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355258} {:answer/id #uuid "f36579c1-a15a-5c9c-86e5-d88683ef116b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355259} {:answer/id #uuid "94fadcec-2ce2-504e-bd6f-b14622da91c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=y\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94fadcec-2ce2-504e-bd6f-b14622da91c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=y\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355260} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d79e42d-26ef-5da0-ae53-884ba9501d93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77a95e06-f7ce-5b85-aec6-d39c67229989" :question/math-academy-id "q-122633" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/251e49513353092b4f9a16f54bb14fbaa1afe1a14e5fecf5b3ce54905fed474d.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=y\\,i+j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' horizontal components (i.e., the $i$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=x\\,i,\\,K(x,y)=-i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=y\\,i.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "888aa30d-7179-507c-a30c-38209587333b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Three-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "669cdc44-e59b-5fdd-b4e8-7550dbc0ca53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355263} {:answer/id #uuid "92e83f43-4dcd-57b6-8ff1-bc7bdb0da4f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=i+x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355264} {:answer/id #uuid "20ae3332-e4da-5ccb-be37-8406508b63a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355265} {:answer/id #uuid "dace7325-420a-5fbf-a4c6-57a9e8bca39d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=2\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355266} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad084bf-dd80-54aa-927e-ed1e36697e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=x\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dace7325-420a-5fbf-a4c6-57a9e8bca39d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=2\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355266} :answer-field/id #uuid "661f6eb5-5993-5f29-a557-6886a5aca132" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31270881-eb16-5f34-9cb7-b40b052fc37e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122651" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/7cb4dd61f9d42a48c022a183e7f4310a8a4ed7ae881edd136881ef6863282e2c.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $x$-axis. So, the $j$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=i+x\\,j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=-i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=x\\,i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y,z)=2\\,i.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "888aa30d-7179-507c-a30c-38209587333b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Three-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bca0d8-fc44-5eb7-b2aa-805fe0fab08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355270} {:answer/id #uuid "0f17a9bc-b6c0-5764-9b0a-50efbcb0dfa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355271} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebf4fc3-22b7-5de5-88d6-992e1fbc5fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355272} {:answer/id #uuid "81e3b2c1-267e-5ed5-b025-8f653c93fd4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355273} {:answer/id #uuid "43ae4009-8ad5-5429-9309-0a024fc13cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e3b2c1-267e-5ed5-b025-8f653c93fd4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355273} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0520932-b57b-5bb1-80e8-9cdb1f097c41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dff92f63-26a7-59f0-940d-e453200180e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122670" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/64f02fa7dcd23b20e61801c0453d8fe7ed013936572e1ee63f748361edd4dec5.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $z$-axis. So, the $i$ and $j$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=i,\\,G(x,y,z)=-j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $z$-direction, so the $k$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=k\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $k$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "888aa30d-7179-507c-a30c-38209587333b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Three-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a59f5d2-c9c3-5cf7-8207-21fe2dc86727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=-{e}^{y}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355277} {:answer/id #uuid "158c228f-5bf9-5767-afa0-73f0d5609088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355278} {:answer/id #uuid "4612f4f0-da8b-5c19-bb63-ffc59a5e2cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=-2\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355279} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e1b7d1-9d13-5d64-af17-ee141dcf9ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355280} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5ce636-0258-5495-8056-6a9fc8b574d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=-\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158c228f-5bf9-5767-afa0-73f0d5609088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355278} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a8971a-f8ea-53f9-b748-137a7dacbf31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee80faae-e2ae-56d9-a095-c6a1bfb37ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-123750" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/cfc15b6202167211b7d6c0e8f6635dd9e571810d5296a209a4c317350604c4a4.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $x$-axis. So, the $j$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=i-j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=-2\\,i,\\,H(x,y,z)=-\\,i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{e}^{y}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields."}]}
